 "body": {
  "model": "openai/text-embedding-3-small",
  "input": "Why do notifier consumers commit offsets every five seconds?\n[2025-02-11] incident-review/INC-2025-004: Review of INC-2025-004 (the notifier, 2025-02-06). The root cause was a consumer offset stuck after a broker restart. We decided that notifier consumers will commit offsets every five seconds, because a stuck offset went unnoticed for 40 minutes during INC-2025-004. [2025-02-20] standup/boreal/2025-02-20: Decided in today's standup: the notifier will retry failed pushes three times with exponential backoff, since the flat one-second retry was hammering the push provider during its outages. [2025-07-03] standup/atlas/2025-07-03-2: Atlas saw that the notifier's memory use grew steadily for a week following the cache change; not their service, so they flagged it. The Atlas team noticed that the resizer's cold start time tripled after the runtime upgrade and pinged the owners.",
  "dimensions": 1536
 },
